(COMMERCIAL PROPERTY LEASE) Tj T*
(Lease Reference HP-L-2026-0037) Tj T*
T*
(This Lease is made on March 9, 2026 between Harbour Point Estates Limited, a company) Tj T*
(registered in England and Wales with its registered office at 14 Dockside Row, Bristol BS1) Tj T*
(5TY \("Landlord"\), and Calder & Fenn Bookbinders Ltd, a company registered in England and) Tj T*
(Wales with its registered office at 9 Maltings Lane, Bath BA1 2QR \("Tenant"\).) Tj T*
T*
(1. Demised Premises. The Landlord lets to the Tenant the ground-floor workshop unit known as) Tj T*
(Unit 4, Harbour Point Industrial Estate, together with the loading bay immediately adjoining) Tj T*
(it and the right to use six marked parking spaces.) Tj T*
T*
(2. Term and Rent. The term is ten \(10\) years from the Commencement Date. The initial annual) Tj T*
(rent is forty-eight thousand pounds \(GBP 48,000\), payable quarterly in advance on the usual) Tj T*
(quarter days, subject to upward-only review on the fifth anniversary.) Tj T*
T*
(3. Rent Review. The reviewed rent is the open market rent of the Premises on the review) Tj T*
(date, assuming a willing landlord and willing tenant and a term equal to the residue of the) Tj T*
(term, disregarding any goodwill attributable to the Tenant's business.) Tj T*
T*
(4. Repair. The Tenant shall keep the Premises in good and substantial repair and condition,) Tj T*
(damage by insured risks excepted, and shall yield up the Premises in that condition at the) Tj T*
(end of the term.) Tj T*
T*
(5. Alterations. The Tenant shall not make structural alterations. Non-structural alterations) Tj T*
(require the Landlord's prior written consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld or) Tj T*
(delayed.) Tj T*
T*
(6. Insurance. The Landlord shall insure the Premises against loss or damage by the insured) Tj T*
(risks and the Tenant shall reimburse the premium as additional rent within fourteen \(14\)) Tj T*
(days of demand.) Tj T*
T*
(7. Assignment and Subletting. The Tenant shall not assign, underlet or part with possession) Tj T*
(of part only of the Premises. Assignment of the whole requires the Landlord's consent under) Tj T*
(section 19\(1A\) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1927.) Tj T*
T*
(8. Forfeiture. If the rent remains unpaid for twenty-one \(21\) days after becoming due, or if) Tj T*
(the Tenant breaches any other obligation, the Landlord may re-enter the Premises and the) Tj T*
(term shall absolutely determine.) Tj T*
T*
(9. Notices. Notices must be in writing and delivered by hand or sent by recorded delivery to) Tj T*
(the addresses above, or to such other address as a party notifies in writing.) Tj T*
T*
(10. Governing Law. This Lease and any dispute arising out of it are governed by the laws of) Tj T*
(England and Wales, and the parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of) Tj T*
(England and Wales.) Tj T*
